REGEDIT4

; Descent 3 - fleet install.reg
; ===============================================================
; Every value here was EXPORTED FROM A BOX, not guessed. box-123
; walked the whole first-run chain by hand on .123 - "Welcome to
; Descent 3!" -> "Multiplayer Profanity Filter Settings" ->
; "Detail Level Setting Not Configured" -> "No Rendering Device
; Selected!" - using the game's own Setup > Speed > Detect System
; Properties and Setup > Video > Scan for the Selected Video
; Devices, then read the registry back. This is that result.
;
; The four *Configured / *Settings flags are the ones that silence
; the wizard; without them an unattended box stops on four modals
; before it ever renders.
;
; PreferredRenderer=3 is Direct3D. RenderingDeviceName is what the
; game's own scan chose on a Radeon; it is the generic primary
; device name rather than a card-specific string, but if a box
; ever renders wrongly, that is the first value to suspect -
; re-run Setup > Video > Scan there and send the difference.
; PredefDetailSetting is deliberately NOT here (removed 2026-10-02).
; main.exe reads the per-option detail values and THEN applies this
; preset (0-3) over all of them; 4 = custom keeps them. A staged 1
; therefore threw away every box's own detail choice at each sync -
; .124's maxed custom detail went to medium. Absent, main.exe
; defaults to medium (DETAIL_LEVEL_MED, init.cpp LoadGameSettings in
; the released source) - what the staged 1 gave a fresh box anyway.
; DetailLevelConfigured stays: it is the D3Launch stub's flag.
; Default_pilot (2026-10-02): the staged pilot sdf.plt carries the
; user's control mapping (WASD + F, mouse - set up by hand on .124 and
; staged from there; the mapping lives IN the pilot) and a 4096x4096
; game window, so the view fills any display (provisioning/patches/
; descent3). This value only PRE-SELECTS it in the PILOTS menu; the
; Play and Join launchers pass -pilot SDF, which skips that menu.
; 3Dfx Glide was deliberately unchecked: no fleet box has had a
; Voodoo since 2026-08-11.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Outrage\Descent3]
"ProfanityPrevention"=dword:00000000
"StraightToSetup"=dword:00000000
"DetailLevelConfigured"=dword:00000001
"VideoDetectSettings"=dword:00000001
"PreferredRenderer"=dword:00000003
"RenderingDeviceName"="Primary Display Driver"
"RS_vsync"=dword:00000001
"net directory"=""
"Default_pilot"="sdf.plt"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Outrage\Descent3\Version]
"Major"=dword:00000001
"Minor"=dword:00000004
"Build"=dword:00000000

; Version updated 1.0.0 -> 1.4.0 when the official 1.4 file set from
; http://descent3.com/patch/ was applied to this tree (29 files, per the
; vendor's own patch.bat). The tree also now carries version.new, which is the
; file the patch itself uses to declare the version - "Convert Version to
; 1.4.0". Both are kept in step deliberately: the registry value is what an
; installer or a patcher reads to decide whether a patch applies, and leaving
; it at 1.0.0 would invite a later patch run to "upgrade" an already-current
; tree.
